# 310: §4 / §6 `.36`. Unbounded recursion is a `Value` error naming the limit,
# never a stack overflow. Depth is ACTIVE INVOCATIONS with the top level at 0 and
# the check is `depth == 1000` at the call site, so invocations 1..1000 succeed
# and the 1001st fails. The line is the failing CALL's line — 2, the recursive
# call inside the body, not 5 where the top-level call is. Output printed before
# the recursion is kept.
--- source
fn down(n) {
  return down(n + 1);
}
print "go";
print down(1);
--- expect
go
error: Value at line 2: recursion limit of 1000 frames exceeded
